For example, when checking if "radar" is a palindrome, we start by comparing characters from the beginning and end of the string, moving towards the center. Since "r-d-a-r" is a palindrome, our function returns true.

Note that these methods have different time complexities: O(n) for `isPalindrome(String s)` and `isPalindrome(int[] nums)`, where n is the length of the string or array; O(n/2) for `isPalindrome(String s, int start, int end)` and `isPalindrome(int[] nums, int start, int end)`.
